IMPORTANT:
  * By default, copyright law treats this repository as
    "All Rights Reserved" (proprietary). Other people may view the
    code on GitHub, but they do NOT automatically have the right to
    copy, modify, or redistribute it.

  * If you want others to be able to use, modify, and share your
    work, replace THIS file with a real license. Common choices for
    an Embedded C / academic project:

      - MIT License        -> permissive, simple, widely used.
                               Good default for portfolio projects.
      - Apache License 2.0 -> permissive, adds an explicit patent grant.
      - GNU GPLv3          -> copyleft; derivative works must also
                               stay open source under the GPL.

  * To add a license on GitHub without editing files manually:
    On your repository page click  "Add file" -> "Create new file",
    type the file name  LICENSE,  and GitHub will show a "Choose a
    license template" button.

Until a real license is added, treat all source code in this
repository as copyrighted and not licensed for redistribution.

